## Authorization and destructive actions

Describe who can approve writes, deploys, migrations, data deletion, force pushes, or other irreversible actions. Require an explicit, reviewable step for destructive operations and record the actor and evidence.

## Isolation

State whether a branch, Git worktree, container, or remote worker provides isolation. A worktree isolates source changes but does not isolate processes, network access, credentials, ignored files, or external services.

